<concept id="contract_document_versions_07b77f" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Contract Document Versions</title>
     <shortdesc>When you check in documents from X-Author, document versions are incremented based on Contract Document</shortdesc>
   <prolog>
      <author type="creator">Chris Castro</author>
      <critdates>
         <revised modified="Oct 10, 2016"/>
      </critdates>
       <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>rating</keyword>
        <keyword>display</keyword>
        <keyword>Filter</keyword>
        <keyword>include</keyword>
        <keyword>placeholder</keyword>
        <keyword>version</keyword>
        <indexterm>rating</indexterm>
        <indexterm>display</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Filter</indexterm>
      </keywords>
          <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <conbody><p>When you check in documents from X-Author, document versions are incremented based on Contract Document Versioning. For example, if you work with version 1.0.0 (the first generated draft of an agreement), and check it in as a new redlined version, the version of the document increments to a new "negotiator" version, version 1.1.0. The following section describes how Contract Document Versioning works. Keep in mind that minor (reviewer) versions cannot be created from the X-Author client but that you may work potentially check out reviewer versions as part of the negotiation process.</p>
